  "description": "Null versus empty Text on one variable field. Row 7 has T.N Null and T.V = 'v7' (V allows zero length, N is a DDL default). Steps: V to the empty string; V to Null; V to a value; then an attempt to store the empty string in N. Asks how presence differs between Null and empty in the closed file and which attempt the engine refuses. Images: 'before' (the fixture copy as given), then one kept image of the closed file after each step; every step opens the database read/write, makes one mutation and closes it.",
